  "interpretation": "Phase F2 re-measure on pokemon-lore/kanto (same protocol: 20 docs, seed 0, qwen/qwen3-32b /no_think, ontology-predicate-constrained). RAW coverage under the Phase F estimand is 0.1053 (44/418); the prior Phase F receipt reported ~0.1391 on a separate judge draw \u2014 same failure class, judge-draw variance expected. CLEAN coverage (manifest-validated, in-unit, id_map-canonical-matched) is 0.3103 (36/116). Of 418 raw assertions, 193 (46%) were judge_rejected (type-invalid / non-manifest shape \u2014 e.g. occurs_at\u2192weekday, involves\u2192non-entity), 109 (26%) were out_of_unit (subjects outside the kanto 15_structured entity set + global: rule \u2014 cross-region content on cross-region pages is a corpus-composition finding, not an extraction gap), and 116 remained in-scope. In-scope hits split by match_mode: exact=35, soft-object=1, canonical=0 (canonical recovered no additional hits on this draw \u2014 the matcher class was small vs type/scope noise). Metric noise therefore accounts for ~72% of the raw denominator; after removing it the real extraction gap is still large (80 misses / 116 in-scope = 69% miss rate, clean coverage 0.31 << gate 0.6). Verdict: FAIL on the clean number the improve loop and certificate will cite; mitigation remains a second extraction pass (and/or corpus de-scoping of cross-region pages), not a training iteration.",
